      "farewell": "Wrote answer_1318992729.preql and validated it with --run.\n\nQuery:\n  import root.Agreement_Party_Role as apr;\n  where apr.party_role_code = 'AG'\n  select apr.party_identifier, count(apr.agreement_identifier) as policies_sold;\n\nResult (1 row): party_identifier = 2, policies_sold = 2.\n\nRationale: Agreement_Party_Role links each policy/agreement to its parties with a role code (AG = agent, PH = policyholder). Filtering to the agent role and counting agreements per agent party gives the number of policies each agent sold. The agent party (id 2) is the AG on both agreements, so it sold 2 policies.",
